From 9f014a21c3a36a687524ce6050be731b7bdbd702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:36:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(browser): managed leases bind supervisors, sidecars and
 vault scope [daveey]

Addresses the gpt-6-astra review of the managed all-tools lease change:
- supervisor_in_scope: inside a tool lease or a vault operation, a cached CDP
  supervisor attached through another endpoint (older capability or a
  pre-activation raw attach) is never used: dialog/cdp-frame refuse with a
  reopen hint, eval fast path and snapshot merge fall through, the vault treats
  it as absent; _ensure_cdp_supervisor outside a lease only trusts a session own
  leased URL.
- A retained hybrid sidecar never launches local Chrome under a managed lease:
  clear error, binding dropped so the next call uses the managed session.
- renew_selected pins the vault scope for the whole operation (ContextVar read
  by supervisor_task), so a concurrent browser_exec cannot redirect a fill.
- Missing task identity is refused under managed config instead of sharing a
  default owner; unmanaged keeps the default.
---
